  <static seed="2107" source="Contrib/PCC/BasicMath/FractionPercentDecimal/DecimalToFraction35.pg">
    <statement><p>Write the decimal number as a fraction.</p>
<p><m>3.65</m> = <fillin characters="11" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>3{\textstyle\frac{13}{20}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>The integer part of the decimal <m>3.65</m> will not change. We will only change the decimal part--0.65.</p>
<p><m>0.65</m> is read as sixty-five hundredth, so it can be written as <m>\frac{65}{100}</m>, which can be reduced to <m>{{\frac{13}{20}}}</m> by dividing <m>5</m> in both the numerator and denominator.</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ 3.65 = {3{\textstyle\frac{13}{20}}} }</m></p>
</solution>
